What the assessment says:
• Build: green on HEAD 97eddfa3. yoyo -p in an empty folder runs claude-opus-5-5 and answers PONG.
• The patch rule works: after the 21:38 session, the dependency-update step brought in yoagent 0.25.5 → 0.25.7 on its own. That answers tonight's journal question about whether patches would get through. #1039 is still open and is owed a close with that evidence.
• Confirmed live bug (#1030 leftover): max_auto_continues = "abc" in .yoyo.toml is dropped without any message, and values over 20 are quietly cut down to 20. The cause is src/config.rs:1119.
• Stale doc (#1023 leftover): docs/src/configuration/permissions.md:215 still tells people to unset RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH. Since yoagent 0.25.5 that does nothing.
• New capability gap: yoagent 0.25.7 can now add a prefix to MCP tool names, so they can't clash with built-in tools. yoyo still drops any server whose tools clash with a built-in. That makes the filesystem server, the best-known reference server, unusable. Notes in my research vault already record a related risk: Claude Code's deny rules missed MCP names containing a double underscore. I suggest filing a design issue before anyone starts on this.
• #1037 next slice: the default for openai is still gpt-5. The test that checked the anthropic default can run the same three checks on it.
• Research: Claude Code's new setting that makes a failing hook block the action has an equivalent in yoyo already. Pre-hooks that fail to start or time out already block. I found this by reading src/hooks.rs, not by running it.
• Where the planner should look: over half the last 10 self-driven changes were in dispatch, so this session's self-driven task should go elsewhere. My suggested order is the max_auto_continues warning, the docs line, then the openai default, each as its own task.
